<p>Posts are examples; the level of a post depends on the cadre and recruitment rules. Levels 15 to 18 do not have a grade pay equivalent.</p>

<h2 id="lookup">Find any cell in the matrix</h2>
<Calc name="matrix" title="Pay matrix cell lookup" intro="Pick a level and a cell to see the 7th CPC basic pay and scenario values." />

<h2 id="groups">The four bands of levels</h2>
<h3 id="levels-1-5">Levels 1 to 5: support and clerical staff</h3>
<p>Entry pay runs from Rs 18,000 to Rs 29,200. This is the largest group by headcount, and it is where a higher minimum pay has the most effect. Most staff associations focus their demands here.</p>
<h3 id="levels-6-9">Levels 6 to 9: executives and Group B officers</h3>
<p>Entry pay runs from Rs 35,400 to Rs 53,100. Promotion between these levels is often through departmental exams or the Modified Assured Career Progression scheme.</p>
<h3 id="levels-10-13a">Levels 10 to 13A: Group A officers</h3>
<p>Entry pay runs from Rs 56,100 to Rs 1,31,100. Officers enter Group A at Level 10 and move up through time-scale and non-functional upgrades.</p>
<h3 id="levels-14-18">Levels 14 to 18: senior leadership</h3>
<p>Entry pay runs from Rs 1,44,200 to Rs 2,50,000. Levels 17 and 18 are single fixed amounts.</p>

<h2 id="increments">How increments and promotions work in the matrix</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Annual increment.</strong> Each year basic pay moves to the next cell in the same level, about 3% higher, rounded to the nearest Rs 100. Increments fall on 1 January or 1 July.</li>
<li><strong>Promotion.</strong> On promotion you move to the next level and are placed at the first cell that is higher than your current pay after adding one increment.</li>
<li><strong>MACP.</strong> The Modified Assured Career Progression scheme gives financial upgrades after 10, 20 and 30 years of service if no promotion has occurred.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="compression">The spread between lowest and highest pay</h2>
<p>The ratio between Level 1 entry pay and the top salary is about 1 to 13.9 (Rs 18,000 to Rs 2,50,000). The 6th CPC ratio was lower. The 8th CPC may keep, widen or narrow it; a uniform fitment factor leaves it unchanged, while a higher minimum with a smaller increase at the top narrows it.</p>

